@startuml Key Generation Flow
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #ffffff
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

participant "Application" as app
participant "@noble/curves" as noble
participant "Secure Storage" as storage
database "Keychain/KeyStore" as ks

== Key Generation Flow ==

app -> noble: randomPrivateKey()
note right of noble
  Generate 32 bytes of
  cryptographically secure entropy
  from crypto.getRandomValues()
end note

noble -> noble: Validate entropy\n(1 ≤ key < curve order)
noble --> app: privateKey (32 bytes)

app -> noble: getPublicKey(privateKey, false)
note right of noble
  Derive public key from private key
  Uncompressed format:
  0x04 + x (32 bytes) + y (32 bytes)
end note
noble --> app: publicKey (65 bytes)

app -> app: Convert to JWK format
note right of app
  Extract x and y coordinates
  Base64url encode
  Create RFC 7517 JWK object
end note
app -> app: Generate keyId\n"key-{first8hex}"

== Storage ==

app -> storage: storePrivateKey(keyId, privateKeyHex)
storage -> ks: Keychain.setGenericPassword()
note right of ks
  iOS: Keychain + Secure Enclave
  Android: KeyStore + StrongBox/TEE
  Private key never returned
end note
ks --> storage: Success
storage --> app: Done

== Return ==

app --> app: Return {publicKeyJwk, keyId}
note right of app
  Public key and keyId sent to caller
  Private key remains in secure storage
  Never accessible to application
end note

@enduml
